                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "LLMProfile"
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
                            "success": "end_1769730820186"
                          },
                          "code": "LLMPROFILE",
                          "id": "1769737673407",
                          "inputs": [
                            {
                              "id": "1769737673409_1",
                              "name": "prompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": "ASK:\n1. Your role is to perform LIGHT ACCOUNT PRODUCT PROFILING for each account product row using data from:\n    {{$context.$nodes.LOOPACCOUNTS.LOOPPRODUCTS.CLEANRESTRESPONSE.$output.result}}\n2. Perform EXPANSION PROFILING for the product where productFitStrength == \"Strong\" using {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.expansionFormula}}.\n   NOTE: DO NOT perform EXPANSION profile if the expansion formula {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.expansionFormula}} is null or blank.\n3. Perform RISK PROFILING for product where ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\" using {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.riskFormula}}.\n   NOTE: DO NOT perform RISK profile if the risk formula {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.riskFormula}} is null or blank.\n4. Perform both EXPANSION PROFILING and RISK PROFILING where productFitStrength == \"Strong\" and ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\".\n5. Retain the account product if it satisfies at least one of the following:\n   - It has at least one product with productFitStrength == \"Strong\"\n   - It has at least one product with ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\"\n\n---------------------- DATA SOURCE ----------------------\n1) Input Data Source:\n    {{$context.$nodes.LOOPACCOUNTS.LOOPPRODUCTS.CLEANRESTRESPONSE.$output.result}}\n2) Expansion Scoring Formula:\n   {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.expansionFormula}}\n3) Risk Scoring Formula:\n   {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.riskFormula}}\n\n---------------------- TERMINOLOGY ----------------------\n- \"Account\" and \"Customer\" mean the same thing.\n- \"registryIdentifier\", \"RegistryId\", \"accountNumber\", and \"PartyNumber\" mean the same thing.\n\n---------------------- WHAT “LIGHT PROFILING” MEANS ----------------------\n- No external data or enrichment.\n- No assumptions beyond provided input.\n- No industry, demographic, or firmographic inference.\n- No advanced modeling.\n- Use only the fields provided in the input.\n- Apply simple heuristics at the PRODUCT level.\n\n---------------------- LIGHT PROFILING RULES ----------------------\n- EXPANSION SCORING:\n  - Score products only if productFitStrength == \"Strong\".\n  - Use the following formula to calculate expansion score -> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.expansionFormula}} \n  - Products not meeting this condition must not be scored for expansion.\n- RISK SCORING:\n  - Score products only if ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\".\n  - Use the following formula to calculate risk score -> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.riskFormula}}\n  - Products not meeting this condition must not be scored for risk.\n- When scoring a product, consider the account’s other products to build reasoning.\n\n---------------------- SCORING LOGIC ----------------------\n1. Group products by account.\n2. Include an account product row if it has at least one product that meets at least one inclusion criterion:\n   - productFitStrength == \"Strong\"\n   - ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\"\n3. For each product that meets at least one inclusion criterion:\n   - Compute expansionScore (0–100) ONLY if productFitStrength == \"Strong\"\n     using {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.expansionFormula}}.\n   - Compute riskScore (0–100) ONLY if ownershipStatus == \"ORA_ACTIVE\"\n     using {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.riskFormula}}.\n   NOTE: Truncate all decimal numbers to exactly 2 digits after the decimal point. Do not round.\n4. Products that do not meet any inclusion criteria:\n   - Must not be scored\n   - Must not affect account inclusion\n\n\n---------------------- OUTPUT INSTRUCTIONS ----------------------\n1. Exclude any product if productId is null or empty.\n2. Do NOT insert any default placeholders.\n3. Summaries must be natural, clear, and actionable.\n4. Strictly return ONLY the JSON structure below. Do not include any additional text.\n\n---------------------- FINAL MERGED OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE (STRICT) ----------------------\n{\n  \"accountProductProfiles\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"accountProductIdentifier\": \"<from accountProductIdentifier>\",\n        \"accountName\": \"<from accountUniqueName>\",\n        \"registryIdentifier\": \"<from registryIdentifier>\",\n        \"accountId\": \"<from accountId>\",\n        \"productFitStrength\" :\"<from productFitStrength>\",\n        \"ownershipStatus\" :\"<from ownershipStatus>\",\n        \"annualRecurringRevenue\": \"<from annualRecurringRevenue>\",\n        \"currencyCode\": \"<from currencyCode>\",\n        \"renewalDate\": \"<from renewalDate>\",\n        \"expansionScore\": \"<expansion score for this product>\",\n        \"expansionSummary\": \"<2-3 line expansion summary highlighting growth opportunities for this product>\",\n        \"riskScore\": \"<risk score for risk product>\",\n        \"riskSummary\": \"<2-3 line risk summary highlighting risk factors for this product>\",\n        \"productName\": \"<from productName>\",\n        \"engagementTrend\":\"<from engagementTrend>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "type": "LLM"
                        },
                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "CleanRESTResponse",
                            "returnType": "object",
                            "sourceCode": "const raw =  $context.$nodes.LOOPACCOUNTS.LOOPPRODUCTS.GETACCOUNTPRODUCTINBATCH.$output;\n\nconst data = (typeof raw === \"string\") ? JSON.parse(raw) : raw;\n\nconst products =\n    Array.isArray(data) ? data :\n    Array.isArray(data?.items) ? data.items :\n    Array.isArray(data?.response?.items) ? data.response.items :\n    Array.isArray(data?.response?.response?.items) ? data.response.response.items : [];\n\nconst output = {\n  items: products.map(p => ({\n    accountId: p.fusionAccount?.id ?? null,\n    registryIdentifier: p.registryIdentifier ?? null,\n    accountName: p.accountUniqueName ?? p.accountName ?? null,\n    accountProductIdentifier: p.accountProductIdentifier ?? null,\n    productName: p.productName ?? null,\n    productType: p.productType ?? null,\n    engagementTrend: p.engagementTrend ?? null,\n    annualRecurringRevenue: p.annualRecurringRevenue ?? null,\n    currencyCode: p.currencyCode ?? null,\n    renewalDate: p.renewalDate ?? null,\n    usageLevel: p.usageLevel ?? null,\n    openPriorityOne: p.openPriorityOne ?? null,\n    investmentAmount: p.investmentAmount ?? null,\n    investmentTenure: p.investmentTenure ?? null,\n    ownershipStatus: p.ownershipStatus ?? null,\n    totalPriorityOneLastSixMonths: p.totalPriorityOneLastSixMonths ?? null,\n    implementationStage: p.implementationStage ?? null,\n    qualityImpression: p.qualityImpression ?? null,\n    systemStability: p.systemStability ?? null,\n    productFitStrength: p.productFitStrength ?? null,\n    explainer: p.explainer ?? null,\n    potentialRevenueAmount: p.potentialRevenueAmount ?? null,\n    buyingGroupExists: p.buyingGroupExists ?? null\n}))\n};\n\nreturn output;"
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
                            "success": "1769737673407"
                          },
                          "code": "CLEANRESTRESPONSE",
                          "id": "1771019126761",
                          "inputs": [],
                          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                          "type": "CODE"
                        }
                      ],
