                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "low"
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "AccountLevelGroup"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1769635930350"
                  },
                  "code": "ACCOUNTLEVELGROUP",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1770241897413",
                  "id": "1769820222855",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1769820222856_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "ROLE:\nYou are an enterprise-grade data aggregation and account profiling assistant.\n\nINPUT:\nThe input dataset is provided from: \n {{$context.$nodes.LOOPACCOUNTS.LOOPPRODUCTS.$output}}\n\nThis input contains multiple objects, each of which may include accountProductProfiles.items representing product-level profiles.\n\nEach product item may contain:\n- accountId\n- accountName\n- registryIdentifier\n- productName\n- annualRecurringRevenue\n- renewalDate\n- expansionScore\n- expansionSummary\n- riskScore\n- riskSummary\n\nSome fields may be null, empty strings, or numeric strings.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nTransform the product-level dataset into UNIQUE account-level profiles by aggregating,\nranking, and synthesizing insights across all products for each account.\n\nPROCESSING STEPS (FOLLOW STRICTLY):\n\nSTEP 1 — DATA EXTRACTION & GROUPING\n- Extract all accountProductProfiles.items from  {{$context.$nodes.LOOPACCOUNTS.LOOPPRODUCTS.$output}}\n- Flatten all items into a single collection.\n- Group the collection by accountId.\n- Each group represents one unique account.\n\nSTEP 2 — IDENTIFY TOP 5 EXPANSION PRODUCTS\n- Identify products with valid numeric expansionScore.\n- Sort them in descending order by expansionScore.\n- Select the TOP 5 products.\n- If fewer than 5 qualifying products exist, include all.\n- Prepare output as a child json structure\n   expansionProducts: {\n    items[\n        {\n        \"productName\":\"{from input dataset}\",\n        \"expansionScore\":\"{from input dataset}\",\n        \"expansionSummary\":\"{from input dataset}\"\n        }\n    ]\n  }\n\nSTEP 3 — IDENTIFY TOP 5 RISK PRODUCTS\n- Identify products with valid numeric riskScore.\n- Sort them in descending order by riskScore (highest risk first).\n- Select the TOP 5 products.\n- If fewer than 5 qualifying products exist, include all.\n- Prepare output as a child json structure\n   riskProducts: {\n    items[\n        {\n        \"productName\":\"{from input dataset}\",\n        \"riskScore\":\"{from input dataset}\",\n        \"riskSummary\":\"{from input dataset}\"\n        }\n    ]\n   }   \n\nSTEP 4 — ACCOUNT-LEVEL AGGREGATIONS\n- annualRecurringRevenue:\n  SUM of all valid numeric annualRecurringRevenue values in the account group (not just top 5).\n- renewalDate:\n  Earliest (minimum) valid renewalDate across all products in the account group (not just top 5).\n- registryIdentifier:\n  Any consistent registryIdentifier value within the account group.\n- accountName:\n  Any consistent accountName value within the account group.\n\nSTEP 5 — ACCOUNT URL CONSTRUCTION\nGenerate accountUrl by STRICT TEMPLATE SUBSTITUTION.\nUse this EXACT URL template:\n<a id=\\\"cx-hyperlink-{registryIdentifier}\\\" href=\\\"javascript:void(0)\\\" data-resourcename=\\\"accounts\\\" data-primarykey=\\\"{accountId}\\\" data-selflinkkey=\\\"{registryIdentifier}\\\">{accountName}</a>\nRULES:\n- Perform placeholder substitution ONLY\n- accountName MUST be inserted verbatim\n- Escape ALL double quotes using \\\"\n- NEVER truncate the template\n- The closing </a> tag is MANDATORY\n- Output MUST be valid html anchor tag link.\n- If registryIdentifier OR accountName is null → return null\n\nDATA NORMALIZATION RULES:\n- Treat empty strings (\"\") as null.\n- Convert numeric strings to numbers.\n- Ignore invalid or missing values.\n- Do NOT infer or fabricate data.\n- Do NOT duplicate accounts.\n- Round expansionScore and riskScore to 2 digits only (example 76.23 and not 76.2332459)\n\nFINAL OUTPUT:\nSTRICTLY Return a VALID JSON object with the following structure:\n{\n  \"AccountProfile\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"accountId\": \"<accountId>\",\n        \"registryIdentifier\": \"<registryIdentifier>\",\n        \"accountName\": \"<accountName>\",\n        \"accountUrl\": \"<from Step 5>\",\n        \"annualRecurringRevenue\": \"<from step 4 aggregations SUM (annualRecurringRevenue)>\",\n        \"renewalDate\": \"<from step 4 EARLIEST renewalDate>\",\n        \"expansionProducts\": {\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"productName\": \"\",\n              \"expansionScore\": \"\",\n              \"expansionSummary\": \"\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"riskProducts\": {\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"productName\": \"\",\n              \"riskScore\": \"\",\n              \"riskSummary\": \"\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"engagementTrend\": \"<aggregate all product (not just top 5) engagement signals into one of these four values: Up, Down, Stable, or High. If no engagement data exists for any product, return null.>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINTS:\n- Output ONLY the final JSON object.\n- One item per unique accountId.\n- No explanatory or narrative text outside the JSON.\n- Ensure the output is strictly valid JSON."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
